{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"code","value":"const RUN_ACCEPTED_EVENT: \"run.accepted\" = 'run.accepted';","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/stream-to-response.ts#L454","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/ai/src/stream-to-response.ts:454"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Name of the synthetic "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"CUSTOM"},{"type":"text","value":" chunk a fresh durable producer appends to its\nlog before pulling the first real chunk."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Flushing "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RUN_STARTED"},{"type":"text","value":" (above) makes a run joinable from the instant the\nstream EMITS something — but a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":" whose middleware boots a sandbox\n(create a container, install a CLI) legitimately emits nothing for minutes,\nand during that window the log is empty. Every joiner's empty-log fail-fast\n("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"memoryStream"},{"type":"text","value":"'s first-chunk deadline, the client's rejoin connect deadline)\nthen reads the run as gone — and the client clears its resume pointer, so a\nreload during the boot window permanently orphans a run that is still going."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This marker closes the window: it is appended (and flushed) before the\nproducer stream is first pulled, so a join always finds a first chunk within\nmilliseconds of the run being accepted. Takeover alignment is unaffected — a\njournal replay cannot reproduce the marker, and alignment already skips\nstored "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"CUSTOM"},{"type":"text","value":" chunks as out-of-band for exactly that reason (see\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isBridgeCustomChunk"},{"type":"text","value":" in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-sandbox"},{"type":"text","value":")."}]}],"headings":[]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\nconst RUN_ACCEPTED_EVENT: \"run.accepted\" = 'run.accepted';\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/stream-to-response.ts:454](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/stream-to-response.ts#L454)\n\nName of the synthetic `CUSTOM` chunk a fresh durable producer appends to its\nlog before pulling the first real chunk.\n\nFlushing `RUN_STARTED` (above) makes a run joinable from the instant the\nstream EMITS something — but a `chat()` whose middleware boots a sandbox\n(create a container, install a CLI) legitimately emits nothing for minutes,\nand during that window the log is empty. Every joiner's empty-log fail-fast\n(`memoryStream`'s first-chunk deadline, the client's rejoin connect deadline)\nthen reads the run as gone — and the client clears its resume pointer, so a\nreload during the boot window permanently orphans a run that is still going.\n\nThis marker closes the window: it is appended (and flushed) before the\nproducer stream is first pulled, so a join always finds a first chunk within\nmilliseconds of the run being accepted. Takeover alignment is unaffected — a\njournal replay cannot reproduce the marker, and alignment already skips\nstored `CUSTOM` chunks as out-of-band for exactly that reason (see\n`isBridgeCustomChunk` in `@tanstack/ai-sandbox`).\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: RUN_ACCEPTED_EVENT\ntitle: RUN_ACCEPTED_EVENT\n---\n\n```ts\nconst RUN_ACCEPTED_EVENT: \"run.accepted\" = 'run.accepted';\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/stream-to-response.ts:454](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/stream-to-response.ts#L454)\n\nName of the synthetic `CUSTOM` chunk a fresh durable producer appends to its\nlog before pulling the first real chunk.\n\nFlushing `RUN_STARTED` (above) makes a run joinable from the instant the\nstream EMITS something — but a `chat()` whose middleware boots a sandbox\n(create a container, install a CLI) legitimately emits nothing for minutes,\nand during that window the log is empty. Every joiner's empty-log fail-fast\n(`memoryStream`'s first-chunk deadline, the client's rejoin connect deadline)\nthen reads the run as gone — and the client clears its resume pointer, so a\nreload during the boot window permanently orphans a run that is still going.\n\nThis marker closes the window: it is appended (and flushed) before the\nproducer stream is first pulled, so a join always finds a first chunk within\nmilliseconds of the run being accepted. Takeover alignment is unaffected — a\njournal replay cannot reproduce the marker, and alignment already skips\nstored `CUSTOM` chunks as out-of-band for exactly that reason (see\n`isBridgeCustomChunk` in `@tanstack/ai-sandbox`).\n"}
